 Add a main toolbar at the top; on mobile it collapses into a hamburger button that opens the left-panel content (tree or column names).\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_004_app_layout.md-24-- Body uses a left panel and right panel separated by a draggable splitter on desktop; on mobile the left panel moves into the hamburger menu and the body fills the width.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_004_app_layout.md-25-- Add a status bar (desktop) showing editable info, keyboard status (caps lock, insert) and a running-agents count with a popup listing the running agents.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_004_app_layout.md-26-- Depend on data management ([[F-002]]) for project/card content; this feature only provides the shell and hosts card/tree/editor views.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_004_app_layout.md-27-\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_004_app_layout.md-28-## acceptance criteria\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_004_app_layout.md-29-- The app starts services and loads the last project before the main window is shown.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_004_app_layout.md-30-- Light and dark themes can be toggled from the toolbar and the choice is remembered across restarts.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_004_app_layout.md-31-- On desktop the body shows a left and right panel with a working splitter; on mobile the left panel is reachable from the hamburger menu and the body is full width.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_004_app_layout.md-32-- The main toolbar is shown on desktop and collapses to a hamburger button on mobile.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_004_app_layout.md-33-- The status bar (desktop) shows info, keyboard status (caps lock, insert) and the number of running agents, with a popup listing them.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_004_app_layout.md-34-- The layout adapts correctly between desktop and mobile at the configured breakpoints.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_004_app_layout.md-35-\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_004_app_layout.md-36-## see 